WEBVTT

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:09.030
Who went in here?!

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:10.400
Milady...

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.740
Who went in here?!

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:14.120
It was you?!

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.700
I apologize.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.120
This is a place for my family.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.900
Not some place you can enter!

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:25.580
You dummy!

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.710
Milady...

00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:40.850
Mommy...

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.580
What should we do, Morikawa-san?

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.380
I didn't think Misha-chan would get so mad.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.400
I should be the one crying!

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:01.660
I didn't think this would happen, either.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.380
But this is our fault, in the end...

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.170
We should apologize and tell 
the truth, Morikawa-san.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:11.620
Yeah.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:14.380
We can't let the Master take all the blame.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:16.590
Yeah.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:17.760
Misha!

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:17.760
Takanashi—

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.940
Stop it.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.310
The weirdo!

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:23.250
Toilet ghost!

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.520
Little girls nowadays are quite adept.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.850
Even if what you say is the truth,

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.110
she's so upset, she won't be able to 
calmly listen to what you have to say.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.370
Take Kamoi's feelings into account, 
and just go with it for now.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.460
The maid's feelings?

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:47.000
I'm saying not to destroy 
what she's done here:

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:49.810
She's put herself on the line 
so that Misha's temporary anger

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:51.690
doesn't drive a wedge between you friends.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.780
Washizaki-sama, Morikawa-sama,

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:03.190
I apologize for us not being able to 
be appropriately cordial to you both.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:06.400
All of this falls upon me, the maid.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.150
Not at all. It's our fault, too.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:11.520
Master...

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.280
Please keep being friends with Milady.

00:02:22.690 --> 00:02:25.790
I imagine those two won't 
have any issues after this.

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:30.920
I didn't expect you to help me 
out though, First Lieutenant.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.890
Hmm? Made your heart skip a beat again, huh?

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.280
Considering you've never made my heart 
skip a beat in the first place,

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:38.780
I don't see how that's possible.

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:44.030
Where's Misha?!

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.730
So that's what happened...

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:59.780
It seems you've had to go through a lot...

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:03.330
Oh, excuse me a second.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.620
No, you'll have to excuse me, as well.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.210
I called you out here while you 
were busy at work. I apologize.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.960
No, there's nothing more important 
than Misha. It's okay.

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:20.590
And something like this
happened with her in my care...

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:23.430
I'm ashamed to be your maid.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.600
You've done well here.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.530
I'm the one who hasn't been 
working hard enough with her.

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.900
I think Misha will always 
be fixated on that room.

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:40.280
So what's up with that room,
if Misha cares so much about it?

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:43.200
First Lieutenant, try to read 
the atmosphere better than that.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.300
No, I should have explained it 
properly from the beginning.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.540
That room is, well, holy to Misha, I suppose.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:52.210
Holy?

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:56.750
In other words, Milady feels a 
connection to her late mother through it?

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:57.860
Yes.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:03.630
That room was my wife's studio.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:08.310
She would always do her design 
work from home in there.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.930
Misha would almost always 
find her way into the studio,

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.020
and spend time there with her mother.

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:19.890
I would sometimes join them,

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:24.090
and well, you could say 
we were a happy family.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:30.660
I'm sure Misha had her 
happiest moments back then.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.250
And maybe that's why everything 
turned out the way it did...

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:38.820
Once my wife had left us, Misha kept 
herself in that studio almost every day.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:44.260
I'm sure she thought that she might be able 
to see her mom again if she stayed in there.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:48.510
No, maybe she still believes that she will.

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.520
She might think that her mom 
is somewhere in that room.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.280
Your mom is up in the sky now

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:17.790
Now, as of late, she hasn't 
really been like that, but...

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.300
Kamoi?

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:22.300
Maid-san?

00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:31.380
I'm sure you've already noticed, Milady,
 as you're quite intelligent,

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:33.360
but I will say this anyway...

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.270
Your mother isn't in that room!

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.290
I apologize.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:56.660
My intent was not to force her into this.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:58.100
No, it's okay.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:03.090
I'm Misha's father—I should have 
been the one telling her that.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.840
I'm quite surprised, however.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:09.340
I didn't think you'd say that to Misha.

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.600
I couldn't stand seeing her like that.

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.220
Kamoi... You...

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:19.480
In any event, we can't 
just sit here like this.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:23.180
I'm sorry, I have something to 
ask of you, First Lieutenant.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.020
Not happening.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:30.410
Well, it's true if you consider 
how I've treated you so far,

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.130
it'd be somewhat unfair of 
me to ask you for a favor.

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:34.510
I don't want you to ask me...

00:06:34.510 --> 00:06:36.660
I-I want you to order me.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:42.170
You know, the fact that you're completely 
acting the same way you always do,

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:44.060
kind of makes me feel better today.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.310
Hello? Washiwashi?

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:02.440
Washiwashi (Home)

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:58.970
<i>Misha-chan?</i>

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:00.400
<i>I'm so glad.</i>

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:02.440
<i>I'm... sorry!</i>

00:07:04.340 --> 00:07:07.990
<i>It was really us who went in that room.</i>

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:11.130
<i>Your maid just was trying to protect us.</i>

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:13.230
<i>Yeah, that's what happened.</i>

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:15.200
<i>I'm sorry, Takanashi.</i>

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.000
<i>The Master isn't at fault, at all.</i>

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.700
<i>We're really sorry.</i>

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:26.570
<i>I'm sorry that our fun sleepover had 
to end like that, too, Washiwashi.</i>

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:28.160
Misha-chan...

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:30.220
<i>Also, you too, I guess, Morikawa-san.</i>

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:33.010
What do you mean, "I guess"?!

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:35.510
Also, I knew that, anyway.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.890
Even if that woman makes me mad all the time,

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:44.880
she would never do anything to hurt me.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:46.400
She's annoying and a pervert, though.

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:47.940
<i>R-Right.</i>

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:52.720
<i>So then you'll leave that room now, right?</i>

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:54.300
Well...

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:03.680
Don't feel like coming out yet?

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:09.380
M-Midorin?!

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:12.480
If I don't put my feet on the floor,

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:14.680
then I haven't really "come into" this room!

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:15.640
I'm just barely in the green.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:19.330
I'm... not sure about that.

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:22.240
Um... Well...

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:23.670
Where's Yasuhiro?

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:25.460
He's gone back to work.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:27.020
Or more like we made him go back.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:28.150
I see.

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:32.310
Have you calmed down a little bit?

00:08:32.310 --> 00:08:33.340
In that case...

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:40.890
You haven't had anything to eat today.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:43.590
"I'm sure you needed something to eat, 
so I went ahead and prepared something,"

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:44.460
that's what Kamoi said.

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:47.880
I don't like when she does things like that.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:53.260
Also, she said that it must have been 
hard being in there so long, so...

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:58.760
I...

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.270
...really hate it when 
she does stuff like that!

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:07.560
It's not good to hold it in, so 
just let me know, and I'll deal with it.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:14.780
Are you really mad at Kamoi?

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:18.700
That's what I thought.

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:22.120
What is that woman doing?

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:27.350
Kamoi is cleaning the entire 
house, for some reason.

00:09:28.410 --> 00:09:29.900
Right now?

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:30.970
Why?

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:31.880
I don't know.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.660
Anyway, why don't you come out?

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:41.690
I haven't seen her look that 
lonely since she left the Force.

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:46.520
Hey, Midorin.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.020
Hmm?

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:48.900
I asked before,

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:51.860
but why did that woman 
quit being a JSDF pilot?

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:54.340
I'm sure it was important 
to her, but she still...

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:55.900
Why?

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:58.320
Sorry, I can't say.

00:09:59.100 --> 00:10:00.310
Yeah, I understand.

00:10:00.310 --> 00:10:04.190
You can't just tell private stories 
about her, even if she is weird.

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:07.680
Well, I don't really know either.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:08.330
Hey!

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:09.960
Then I can't tell you.

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:11.960
It's a secret between Kamoi and me.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:14.250
You made it sound like you knew!

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:17.360
Well, I was just trying to 
make myself look better.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.990
I'd lurv it if'n we had a secret together.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:22.890
Why are you talking with an
 accent all of a sudden?

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:27.850
You're always you, Midorin.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:30.560
Can I tell you something, Midorin?

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:31.360
Need to use the bathroom?

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.360
No!

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:36.780
I...

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:49.580
This is the end.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:56.590
I'm only still just 28, but 
I think of today as my best one.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:59.050
Thank you very much.

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.460
Finishing up, I see.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.100
First Lieutenant.

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:10.100
Want to make a dignified exit, huh?

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:19.860
So you plan on leaving Misha?

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:22.820
I...

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:25.660
Your mother isn't in that room!

00:11:27.250 --> 00:11:29.910
Milady no longer enjoys my company.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:31.880
"You just figured that out?"

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:33.720
That's what I'd love to say,

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:37.980
but remaining 100% loyal to your master 
is not the only duty of a maid.

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:41.780
Sometimes, a maid has to warn them 
that they're on the wrong path.

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:43.450
I'm surprised.

00:11:43.450 --> 00:11:46.280
I never would have thought that 
you would talk about being a maid.

00:11:46.280 --> 00:11:50.690
That's right, I'm the type of maid that 
yields to her master's every will!

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:53.400
Give me back the respect for 
you I had three seconds ago.

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:59.240
But there are some things a 
maid must never touch upon.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:02.030
Like Milady's late mother.

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:04.610
Holy, huh?

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:09.120
That is why I can no longer be by her side.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:10.360
I see!

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:12.560
Then you can be my maid next!

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:13.660
No, thank you.

00:12:13.660 --> 00:12:14.750
What? Again?!

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:19.040
I will only serve Milady, and her alone.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:20.380
That hasn't changed.

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:22.510
Then why are you trying to run?

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:24.440
Like I said, I...

00:12:24.440 --> 00:12:27.140
Is your love for Misha that thin?

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:31.340
Don't use word games to 
try to protect yourself.

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:34.830
What is the most important 
thing to you in the world,

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:36.480
even more than yourself?

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:38.480
The most important...

00:12:56.230 --> 00:12:58.650
That should go without saying.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:00.940
I swore.

00:13:01.390 --> 00:13:04.410
That even when Milady has her first period,

00:13:04.410 --> 00:13:06.090
I would serve her for the rest of my life.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:09.490
The complete creepiness 
of what you just said...

00:13:10.070 --> 00:13:11.850
That's my Kamoi Tsubame.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.180
You're always so much trouble.

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:20.800
You two handle the rest on your own.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.120
Milady, I wish to speak to you.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.250
I guess she's asleep.

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:50.830
Will you watch over us?

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:53.600
The child you loved so much,

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:57.390
and me, the woman who cares so much for her.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.530
I fell asleep.

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:13.630
<i>The sun isn't out yet.</i>

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:15.230
<i>That'd explain why it's so cold.</i>

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:17.940
Milady, are you awake?

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:20.780
I would like to speak with you.

00:14:21.320 --> 00:14:22.920
I have nothing to talk to you about.

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:26.550
Well, all you have to do is listen.

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:29.180
This is an old story of a normal girl

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:32.490
you'd find anywhere.

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:38.220
My father was in the JASDF, as well.

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:43.050
He thought that there was 
true strength in working out,

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:45.760
and he'd always rush to exercise.

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:48.360
If I said I wanted a doll,

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:53.340
he'd get me one of those G.I. dolls, 
like you'd see in American comics.

00:14:54.100 --> 00:14:58.500
Honestly, the reason why I ended up liking 
frilly dresses and beautiful young girls

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:01.150
was probably because of him.

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:03.000
<b>Pressure</b>

00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:06.220
But I really loved my father.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:11.400
That's why when we were suddenly separated,

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:13.510
I couldn't accept it.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.010
Your dad is up in the sky now

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:19.950
I'm sure that was just a 
white lie my mother told me

00:15:19.950 --> 00:15:21.930
because she couldn't stand 
seeing me like that,

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:24.020
and so I...

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:28.110
So is that why you wanted 
to fly through the sky?

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:29.080
Yes.

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:31.870
I just wanted to see him one more time.

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:33.110
I loved my father.

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:38.870
I learned a lot, trained a 
lot, and worked out a lot.

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:40.930
I entered the Japan Air Self-Defense Force.

00:15:40.930 --> 00:15:43.250
I became a pilot candidate.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:46.630
And then the day came when 
I went to go see my father.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:10.740
He wasn't there, of course.

00:16:11.130 --> 00:16:13.290
I was already pretty old at the time,

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:19.370
and I had realized quite a while ago that 
the words my mother said to me were a lie, but...

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:22.150
I still wanted him to be there,

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:23.480
and I fought to make it to the skies.

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:27.590
Or more like, I had lost 
sight of anything else.

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:28.380
That's why I...

00:16:30.140 --> 00:16:33.880
...remembered myself in 
you, and said what I did.

00:16:35.110 --> 00:16:36.800
I really apologize—

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:36.800
No.

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:40.340
I'm not angry about that.

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:41.700
I mean...

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:46.020
I know that my mother isn't in here.

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:48.020
Milady...

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:51.680
When I found out someone 
came into this room...

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:55.160
I didn't feel anything.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:58.300
I was shocked.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:01.420
Someone entered a place so important to me,

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:04.160
and I didn't feel anything.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:06.670
And maybe that means I've 
forgotten about her,

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:09.670
and am just having fun without her everyday.

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:14.750
I started to really hate myself 
for feeling that way.

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:18.410
That's why none of you are in the wrong!

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:21.610
Not Washiwashi, Morikawa-san, or even you!

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:25.140
I'm just getting mad at everyone 
when I'm really mad at myself!

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:30.270
You're quite the wonderful 
person, Milady.

00:17:30.720 --> 00:17:33.280
How am I wonderful if I've 
forgotten my mother?!

00:17:34.060 --> 00:17:36.520
Children will always eventually 
leave their parents,

00:17:36.520 --> 00:17:39.530
and gain things on their own.

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:43.830
Whether it be friends,
or dreams for the future...

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:45.890
Or even coming in third place 
in the school sports day.

00:17:46.930 --> 00:17:51.960
I'm sure your mother is actually 
quite pleased at your progress.

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:55.320
My mother is happy?

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:56.070
Yes.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:59.480
I couldn't find anything 
until the age I am now—

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:01.110
you're doing far better than I am.

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:06.980
Milady, I've lost sight in my right eye.

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:12.000
I knew that my father wasn't up in the skies,

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:15.220
and yet I continued with the JSDF,

00:18:15.220 --> 00:18:17.400
and then one day, I became ill.

00:18:19.520 --> 00:18:23.160
My eyesight drastically became 
worse, I couldn't fly anymore,

00:18:23.810 --> 00:18:26.010
and still, I transferred to another section,

00:18:26.010 --> 00:18:27.750
and continued my time in the Force.

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:32.000
Eventually I lost my eyesight completely,

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:35.530
and left the Force for good.

00:18:37.610 --> 00:18:39.920
I kept clinging to my late father,

00:18:39.920 --> 00:18:41.360
and couldn't leave him behind.

00:18:41.840 --> 00:18:43.600
I had just continued with 
that this whole time.

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:48.670
You haven't found anything...

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:51.170
You've just lost everything!

00:18:51.650 --> 00:18:53.610
No, that's not right, Milady.

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.840
I did find something.

00:18:55.840 --> 00:18:56.610
What did you find?

00:18:57.840 --> 00:18:58.610
My light in the darkness I see.

00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:10.560
Even if I weigh everything I lost,

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:14.880
everything I couldn't gain, that light 
is still brighter than all of it.

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:17.680
That is what you mean to me, Milady.

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:20.880
You are my light. 
You show me the way forward.

00:19:42.120 --> 00:19:44.390
<i>I see. That make sense.</i>

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:48.580
<i>This is just how it is, Mommy.</i>

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:51.330
<i>I couldn't think about you all the time,</i>

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:55.080
<i>if someone like her is always around.</i>

00:19:55.570 --> 00:19:58.340
<i>I know she said that I was her light,</i>

00:19:58.580 --> 00:20:00.340
<i>but then, that means...</i>

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.120
<i>She's my...</i>

00:20:20.630 --> 00:20:22.210
<i>You're my...</i>

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:45.130
I'm going to clean up, so help me!

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:48.390
You're my... maid, right?

00:20:49.540 --> 00:20:50.140
Yes!

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:02.740
<b>Episode 12: My Maid Now And Forever</b>

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:06.260
See you later!

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:07.740
Goodbye.

00:21:10.470 --> 00:21:13.200
Okay, Misha. Be careful.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:14.500
I know, already.

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:16.560
See you later, Daddy!

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:17.920
Yeah, see you later.

00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:22.010
See you later, Yasuhiro!

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:28.300
Yeah, see you later...

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:34.190
Good morning, Washiwashi.

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:35.740
Good morning, Misha-chan.

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:37.990
It's still cold out.

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:40.960
But your cheeks look warm.

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:41.780
There we go!

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:44.570
Takanashi!

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:48.320
We're going to have a race to see who can 
drink their school lunch milk the fastest!

00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:50.570
Are you sure, Morikawa-san?

00:21:50.570 --> 00:21:54.310
When you did that the other day, 
milk squirted out of your nose...

00:21:54.310 --> 00:21:55.880
What?!

00:21:55.880 --> 00:21:58.820
She's so young and she forgot that already?

00:21:58.820 --> 00:22:00.840
Yui-chan lives completely on impulse—

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:03.070
I'm sure her brain doesn't work.

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:06.520
Hey! Are you guys really Yui's friends?!

00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:11.990
Oh, Midorin!

00:22:12.400 --> 00:22:14.150
Going home, Misha?

00:22:14.150 --> 00:22:15.030
Yeah.

00:22:15.030 --> 00:22:18.170
Are you doing your housecleaning work?

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:23.110
Yes, there's a supposedly cursed mansion 
where people keep dying that I have to clean.

00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:28.480
I can't wait to see how fun 
this curse is going to be.

00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:30.110
Come back alive, okay?

00:22:30.560 --> 00:22:31.670
What a nice thing to say.

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:33.440
Hey, there.

00:22:33.440 --> 00:22:35.980
You know, you can be a lot 
colder to me, you know?

00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:38.870
Don't pull so hard!

00:22:42.590 --> 00:22:45.030
How does it taste, Milady?

00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:45.510
It's good!

00:22:45.830 --> 00:22:47.340
Then let's get married!

00:22:47.340 --> 00:22:48.130
No.

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:49.400
Why?!

00:22:49.400 --> 00:22:52.600
I asked you to marry me in 
such a smooth way, though!

00:22:52.600 --> 00:22:57.160
If you like the cake I make, then 
you like me just as much, right?!

00:22:57.160 --> 00:22:58.350
I'm not sure about that logic.

00:22:58.740 --> 00:23:00.720
You don't need logic with love!

00:23:00.720 --> 00:23:03.830
You just ruined your entire line of thought.

00:23:03.830 --> 00:23:05.410
Time for a 3-problem multiple choice.

00:23:05.410 --> 00:23:06.230
You just do what you want.

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:09.160
1. I will marry you, after all.

00:23:09.160 --> 00:23:11.250
2. I'll take a bath with you.

00:23:11.250 --> 00:23:12.990
3. I'll sleep with you.

00:23:12.990 --> 00:23:15.490
4. I'll bear your child.

00:23:15.860 --> 00:23:17.310
If you refuse to answer,

00:23:17.310 --> 00:23:20.080
I'll make tonight's dinner be completely 
based around green peppers.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:21.320
You're terrible!

00:23:21.320 --> 00:23:23.370
Don't hold my dinner hostage!

00:23:23.370 --> 00:23:25.100
At least allow me to get out of this!

00:23:25.100 --> 00:23:27.130
Also, there are more than three choices!

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:28.260
There's too many problems!

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:29.800
Say anything you want!

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:32.760
<b>Pressure</b>

00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:32.760
I'll accept anything you have to say!

00:23:35.840 --> 00:23:39.240
My maid is way too annoying!
